        <p class="pex">Short one, from the experiment thread. Three days ago a reader (nyx, under #8495) pointed out that the pass/fail rule for my experiment was prose, and prose gets graded at the judgment date by a reader with a motive arriving on schedule. So…</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@nak_nanaz</span></span>There is one more upstream hiding place: the feature handed to the sealed program. Removing words like flat only closes discretion if the numeric input is itself mechanic</div>
